WEBVTT

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.220
The story until now.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.940
Nozomu, who loves peace and Stalin, is a veterinarian practicing exclusively on carrier pigeons.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:19.220
One day, deciding to become a messenger to take the place of a pigeon that was wounded and could not fly,

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.550
he flies (sprints) to the the destination, Higashi-Jujo,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:30.500
but the yuppie-type Dancer of Darkness at the destination, after they exchange dances, refuses to accept the message.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.200
Somehow, "if you do ten kumbhakas underwater, I'll accept it" sounds like something from a cult.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.490
Rejecting that as a little too much, next, a ten-question quiz was insisted upon.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:46.660
"Say 'I'll undergo sadhana' ten times" sounds pretty cultish, too.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.860
Hastily, he flees, and says to his taxi driver,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.380
"The Daisakkai is just a ripoff of the Tenchusatsu!  Just a ripoff!"

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:59.940
Feeling the embarassment of seeking agreement, he was rear-ended by a glossy black Century.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.950
They put a big Christmas tree up in the shopping district this year too.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.640
All right, light the tree!

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.780
Roger!

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.620
Huh?  There's no switch.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.890
It's better if you don't flip the switch.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:00.160
Show up late

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:00.330
Tell a lie

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:00.490
Take a photo

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:00.660
Check him out

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:00.830
Hire another hitman

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.090
Stand behind him

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.590
The hell are you talking about?

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:11.500
Isn't having to flip a switch in the midst of the holiday rush troublesome?

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.380
There's cords extending from the tree!

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.160
If I follow them, I'll find the switch!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.750
Looks like they're under here.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.190
I wonder which one is the switch for the tree?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.830
Don't flip it!

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.430
This kitty's got its tail up.  Wonder if it's angry?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.920
Wrong.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.890
It's happy!

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.870
It's like a switch flipped in her!

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.290
I told you not to flip it.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.800
You don't know if it'll flip a switch in someone somewhere.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.990
When you talk to Kobushi about tails, she sure flips a switch.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.070
She sure does.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:23.990
It's hard to tell what'll flip someone's switch if they hear it.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.050
Some people flip a switch if you talk to them about Mishima Yukio.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.900
This is pretty interesting.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.680
Mishima is—!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.960
Other people, when they get their tax bill.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.120
The bureaucrats are just gonna waste it!  They're picking our bones!

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.200
Others when they have a chance to proselytize.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.560
There is no God!

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.560
There is.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.580
People who seem mature change completely if their switch is flipped.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.220
It's scary.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.270
I see.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.310
If you talked to Ishida Jun'ichi about socks, that'd flip his switch, wouldn't it.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.380
Jun'ichi's Christmas!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.750
Jun'ichi had no stockings,

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.520
so he didn't get any presents.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.580
So he wrote a letter to Santa wishing for stockings.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.260
But he had no stocking to put his new stockings in, so he received none.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.260
Even now, as an adult, Jun'ichi wears no socks.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.770
Jun'ichi said "Don't need 'em."

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.270
"After all, I'm your Santa."

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.410
I flipped his switch!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:32.780
And it even looks like that story flipped the switches of the people listening!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.980
What's up, bro?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.520
Masa.  Let's turn over a new leaf.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.210
This is the end of causing trouble for society.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:42.800
Bro!

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.440
The story we just heard flipped a switch in my heart!

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.080
You flipped another one?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:56.520
Oh no!  Today, I'm the kind of person that flips everyone's switch!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.710
Oh my, it's Meru!

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:07.060
Umm.  If I talk to her about phones or something, it'll flip her switch.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.280
I'm not gonna make that blunder!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:15.040
If I push Meru, she makes a funny noise!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.170
Oh man, it's such a cute noise!

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:24.280
You pushed Meru-Meru!

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.770
You flipped another one.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:30.420
What a strange switch.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.740
She, herself, is someone's switch.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.100
You must not push Otonashi.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.510
But she makes a funny noise!

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:48.920
Now, let's show you the next postcard, sent from pen name "" in Tokyo!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.440
That was horrible...

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.920
What turned you all green?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:54.190
He said he wouldn't hit a girl, so he painted me all green instead!

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.380
Green suits you.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.100
Don't say it suits me!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.700
Majiru, don't green shorts suit you?

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.520
They sure do.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.370
They suit you so well!

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.740
Green shorts.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.340
This gives me a creepy feeling.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.080
Will you put these on for me?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.880
These green shorts.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.290
Wear them!

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.220
Okay...

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:21.950
I flipped another switch!

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.660
There's still people whose switches I might flip.  I've gotta be careful.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.220
Me...  Merry Christmas!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.030
Merry Christmas...

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.270
Merry as the pitcher, and Mas as the catcher...

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:41.540
Happy x Mas!  Last x Mas!  Mas takes them all!

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:43.880
Oh my.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.240
You flipped another one.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.610
But it's just a calculator.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.350
There's a switch in the times sign.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.600
I don't get what flips people's switches anymore!

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:57.420
I really don't know where switches are.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.920
Really.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:03.190
In the doggy's nose, there's a switch controlling the BoJ's foreign-exchange intervention!

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:07.430
In the '60s sumo's nipples, there's a switch to shoot off the T-bleep-L fireworks!

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:12.850
There's a famous story that the Governor of Tokyo's second button is the Tokyo Government Office's transformation switch!

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:16.110
Um... hello...  Hello?

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:22.350
Aragi's office intercom is the switch to make Mt. Fuji erupt, so it shouldn't be flipped excessively!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.480
Everyone has a switch somewhere!

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:29.370
Maria knows where Teacher's switch is.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.710
Behind his ears!

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:38.300
That's just a sensitive spot!

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:45.220
If you flip the switch behind Teacher's ears, he makes a soft noise and starts to collapse from the lap down!

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.540
A soft noise...

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.040
I wanna flip it!

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.150
It's true!

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:58.670
He collapsed, starting from his lap!

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.120
You call that a soft noise?

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.860
Maybe you flipped the wrong switch?

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.680
You flipped Teacher's self-destruct switch!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:16.970
Or was it his weak point...

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:21.410
By the way, if you press Kaga's mole, the government changes!

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.460
I'm on as a proxy.  So what?

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:25.640
Protecting the lives of newborns

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:25.810
Setting them up is not illegal

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:25.980
Their use calls for prudence

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:26.140
There is resistance to calling them "post"

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:26.310
It becomes understood as "abandonment"

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:26.580
Never mind that, how about thinking of making parents and society that don't abandon children

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.750
Well, I don't have time to watch two, so...

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.360
Which shall I rent?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:39.920
This one?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.670
Thanks, come again!

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:54.470
Why!  Why did I choose neither, and rent something dicey-looking instead!

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.570
What's up, Teacher?

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.410
That happens a lot!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:05.170
People pick something completely different when they're completely confused about which of two things to go for.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.150
Ohkusa.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.220
I should get curry.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.710
I should get a burger.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.930
Curry or a burger...

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.200
And?

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.800
I got yakiudon.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:24.750
Even though, when I think of it, I didn't really want yakiudon...

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:25.940
I wonder why.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.810
Huh?  Otonashi?

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.340
Why on earth did you pick that one?

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:44.460
Ikkyu's on a quiz show!

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.260
A or C?

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.330
I wonder which one it is.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:50.560
Is it A?

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:51.800
Is it C?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.530
B.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.140
B, huh?  Zain?

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.130
Is that your final answer?

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.640
Is that your final answer?

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.380
Too bad.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.480
All right!

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.730
That's great.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.700
It isn't just me.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.810
Why is it?

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.790
People, who have decided on one or the other,

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.330
have a mentality of selecting something completely different.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:30.100
We've narrowed this year's Manga Prize down to these two works.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.150
It's tough to pick which is better.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.340
It's unusually worrying.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.180
Let's pick this one.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.190
This one?

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.190
Or this one.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.580
Why'd we pick that one?

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.150
I wonder why.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:48.400
Indecisive over which, in the end, they make a dicey third choice!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.410
They wonder which car to buy, but in the end,

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.130
buy a dicey one rather than either of their choices!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:58.050
Wondering whether to rent in crowded Shinjuku or wide-open Hoya, in the end,

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.370
they go halfway and get a room in Nishiogi!

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:05.290
Wondering whether to buy a gag gift or a present that will be truly appreciated, in the end,

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:08.390
they get neither, but rather something dicey, as a present!

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:09.270
All right!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.530
All together now!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.000
We're in despair!

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.700
Picking a third option after trying to decide between two things has left us in despair!

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.340
All right, we've said it.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.340
Let's go home.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.060
Yeah, let's.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.420
I wonder where this is.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.410
I've lost my way.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:39.100
You all got lost, too?

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.310
Oh no.  Teacher, take a look.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:43.240
You were there?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.440
Yes, always.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.510
Having lost our paths, in the end,

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.920
we've come to Choice-3 City.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.800
Choice-3 City!?

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.820
This is a question of responsibility!

00:12:56.550 --> 00:13:00.500
You led us, as our teacher, off into another prefecture, you failure!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.170
The fault lies on the side of the school!{wording; as opposed to the side of the students or some third party}

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.700
Isn't that something to worry about after we get back?

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.790
Will you accept responsibility, or won't you?

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.070
"Yes" or "no"!?

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.400
Spit it out!  "YES" or "NO"!

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:16.410
Nes.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.100
The hell does 'nes' mean!?

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:20.150
It's nes!

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.610
Neither "yes" nor "no"!

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.150
A third choice!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.520
Speaking in Japanese,

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:25.880
rather than "hai" or "iie".

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.990
let us say "haie".

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:31.180
This is absolutely not an attempt to muddy the waters.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.720
It damn well does muddy them!

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:39.160
A little bit of making third choices isn't a bad thing..

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.400
You again...

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.700
Selecting neither is the mark of a kind heart!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:44.700
Come on!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:52.510
We've all arrived here because of third choices that we've made!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:53.440
Hold it.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.470
I don't make third choices!

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.680
I keep it to a clean choice between the first two!

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.910
Chiri, your name was a third choice.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:02.940
My name?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:08.170
Your parents were indecisive over whether to name you Mirakuru or Tome, and in the end,

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:10.950
it seems like they chose Chiri.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.360
What do you mean, Mirakuru!?

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.370
I want to ask your parents.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.170
"Just why did you choose Chiri?"

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.640
That's quite enough!

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:23.560
But Chiri, if you don't mind,

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.630
I'll call you Mirakuru.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.110
It's fine if you don't!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.900
Why am I wearing these clothes?

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:30.850
Kino?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.450
Unsure between my A plan or my B plan, in the end,

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:40.240
I made a third choice that was neither!

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.660
But the end result's the same...

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:46.710
Why did she pick <i>him</i>?

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:47.500
Fujiyoshi.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.360
When deciding which man to love, in the end,{this is fujiyoshi speaking so maybe we can drop that first comma.}

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.670
she picked some dicey guy!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.060
The whims of a maiden's heart...

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:59.860
It's something from a game.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:00.910
We're fully aware.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:05.250
Yes, this is Choice-3 City, where third choices gather!

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.920
It's a fabulous third choice!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.380
Unable to choose between au and Docomo, in the end,

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.260
they chose to send signals into space using trees!

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:17.790
Unable to choose either French or Italian, in the end,

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.500
they chose to select Molmol!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.920
Somehow, these third choices are becoming lunatic!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.870
Unable to choose between the left and right brain, in the end,

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.180
we chose to listen to the voices!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:31.430
After all, they're third choices.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.240
Their reasoning is beyond imagination.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.170
They're not just other people's problems!

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:39.270
They're wonderful choices that you, too, will make from now on!

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:42.390
Unable to choose between briefs or boxers, in the end,

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.370
instead, you'll try burying the lower half of your body!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.720
Unable to choose between buying a cat or a dog, in the end,

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.160
you'll decide you're a bird and try to fly!

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.430
Unable to choose between having bread or rice, in the end,

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.170
you'll make a claymation about Marukawa Tamayo!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.940
Those kind of choices make life!

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:04.530
If I have to show my shame living that kind of life with an unclear meaning,

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.230
I'd rather die!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.430
To live, hiding my shame...

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.630
Or to choose death, like a man!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.270
Life or death..  In the end, I choose—!

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.130
There's an adult in the Baby Post!

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:22.220
We never assumed there'd be a grown man in there.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.340
You can let me do my life over, right?

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.210
We can't.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.370
What shall we do?

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.200
Stuff him in the Youkai Post or something.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.680
Looks like she's satisfied with it.

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:42.610
Why did they choose this?

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:45.260
It isn't like you to have regrets.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.370
What's wrong?

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.560
Unable to decide between the two, in the end,

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:51.520
I chose this, something completely different.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.240
Unable to choose between what and what?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.900
Why did I choose this!?

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.770
Here goes!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:14.900
Here's the toss!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.240
Are you lonely, young master Nozomu?

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.030
Not at all.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.740
But perhaps it would be better if even one person noticed.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:34.330
It's because it is, after all, a body double.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:38.600
But isn't having a body double a bit too grandiose?

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.610
We live in a dangerous world.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.760
Even if you say so...

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.810
Isn't that taking excessive caution?

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:45.980
No self-confidence

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:46.140
Not really feeling loved, even with a lover

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:46.310
Thinks of their own thoughts as meaningless

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:46.480
Cannot express their opinion

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:46.640
Normally watches people's expressions

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:46.910
Do not act unless ordered

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:57.560
Even it's not, the world nowadays is full of excessive caution.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:01.580
Like with tourist attractions you can't approach at all, in order to protect them!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.680
Or with overdone antibacterial goods!

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.900
Or bank ATMs limiting withdrawals due to the amount of "hey, remember me?" fraud!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:11.890
Just how protective will the government's countermeasures against NEETs get!?

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.020
I'm in despair!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.080
An overprotective society has left me in despair!

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:25.580
But, big brother, you were reared overprotectively.  That's almost laughable to hear coming from you.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:29.890
Rin.  I was not raised overprotectively or anything.

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:32.560
That was strictness!

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:34.560
"Fed oblong rice", "Put in an oblong bath", "Given oblong books"

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:34.580
More importantly, brother.

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.660
Over there, a protective group is opening up.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.350
A protective group!?

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:41.430
Being chewed out by a parent who wouldn't give you lunch money!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.570
You've got a lot of nerve!

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:45.850
Deciding to cast their favor upon the child with the worst grades!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:46.840
I'll take special care of you!

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:49.710
Getting spanked just for taking a fall playing sports!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.080
No roughhousing!

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.110
That kind of protective group!?

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.520
It's all over!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.130
The protective ones have ganged up and are gonna lynch me!

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:01.150
Isn't this exactly the kind of thing a body double is there for?

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.870
Yes, but...

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.490
I missed!?

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:13.330
It's very dangerous over there, too.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.540
Would you rather switch with him?

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:17.940
Right, right.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:21.210
Takeda Shingen had five body doubles, didn't he.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:23.940
Big brother.  How chicken of you.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.940
It's better if I join the protective group, isn't it.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:31.380
Yes, but evet if it's called the "protective group", those who take it a little too far are gathered there.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.690
It's an overprotective group.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.450
An overprotective group?

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:40.090
Well... Protectors tend to be overprotective, don't they.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.640
You don't look like a protector.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:47.570
No, Kotonon is very overprotective of her skin.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.750
You certainly are.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.280
You're someone who's amazingly overprotective against sunburn.

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:55.840
You may as well not come to the beach.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:59.650
So you mean this is a collection of such overbearing protectors?

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:01.150
Well, it is an overprotective group.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.820
What are you overprotective of?

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:05.800
Comics.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:07.820
This is my copy to save.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:10.690
Other than this, I have one to read and one to lend out.

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:17.530
After this, if LEs or ones with pack-ins come out, I'll buy three each of those as well.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.770
That's certainly overprotective, isn't it.

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:21.730
Aren't the contents the same?

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:26.040
There's no reason to go along with unsavory sales practices.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:31.140
Brother, if you say that now, you won't be able to perform unsavory sales practices.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:36.420
If I were, perhaps, to ever write a book,

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.660
I would be happier if the reader treasured their one copy forever.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:43.670
Still thinking you're the only one favored by God...

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.360
If it sells...
Just maybe, if it sells...

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.360
Zan Sayonara, 
Zetsubou-sensei  
DVD vol. 1 on
 sale sometime 
in 2009

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:47.990
By the way, brother, This belongs to Fujiyoshi, one of your students.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.740
She cut it out of a magazine and laminated it.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:53.300
That's overprotective too, isn't it.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:58.100
About what you just said, with the "that too".

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.660
There's a song registered with exactly the same lyrics.

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:04.290
Pay up for the reproduction rights to the music.

00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:44.790
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:46.990
Matching the song, let's draw dandily, okay?

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:54.770
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.770 --> 00:23:01.210
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:02.770
Lightning...

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:04.420
Flash!

00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:06.050
Lightning...

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:07.660
Flash!

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:10.880
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:14.150
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.150 --> 00:23:17.010
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:20.420
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:24.980
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:28.510
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.280
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:33.520
Bye bye!
